tle transitions between stained glass tableaux.', 'similarity score': 0.5690265893936157}, {'clip_1819_1822': 'clip_1819_1822', 'text': 'This sequence shows the closing production card for **Cosgrove-Hall Productions Ltd.** from their 1980 production (**MCMLXXX**).\n\n**Frames 1-2 (1819-1820s):** The image displays a static, atmospheric shot of a snow-covered Gothic church or cathedral courtyard at night. The scene features Gothic arched doorways, stained glass windows, and an iron street lamp casting light onto the snowy ground. The copyright text "© COSGROVE-HALL PRODUCTIONS LTD. MCMLXXX" is overlaid in a serif font across the lower center of the frame. The mood is wintry, dark, and somewhat Victorian or Dickensian in atmosphere.\n\n**Frames 3-4 (1821-1822s):** The image fades to complete black and remains black for the final two seconds of the sequence.', 'similarity score': 0.5639357566833496}, {'clip_168_171': 'clip_168_171', 'text': 'The sequence opens on a dimly lit, stone-walled interior (168s), suggesting a medieval or rustic dwelling, where a figure in traditional dress stands near a shadowy archway surrounded by pottery and vessels. The scene cuts abruptly to a close-up of a large, dark-furred dog or wolf-like creature snarling aggressively with bared teeth (169s), before shifting to the same animal with its mouth closed and a calmer, almost statuesque expression (170s)—possibly suggesting a transformation or supernatural shift. The final frame (171s) reveals the creature now inside the stone room, moving past hanging cured meats and large storage jars near a dark doorway. Shot in grainy, high-contrast black-and-white with minimal lighting, the sequence creates a tense, ominous atmosphere of impending threat or supernatural horror. No visible text appears in the frames.', 'similarity score': 0.5635921359062195}, {'clip_1106_1109': 'clip_1106_1109', 'text': "**Sequence Description:**\n\n**Frame 1106s:** Two puppet characters peer through a barred window or